(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:symmetry \"Ghost Hacker's three living surfaces now each have the standalone\\n             repo shape ADR-2607011816 established as this franchise's norm:\\n             Ren's line (orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker), SHIRO & PICO's\\n             narrative content (orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico),\\n             and now the game project (orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network)\", :decoupled_from_engine_churn \"isekai-network's lifecycle (design iteration,\\n                                 future concept prototypes) no longer shares a\\n                                 repo, issue tracker, or commit history with\\n                                 kami-engine's in-progress clj-wgsl Rust-removal\\n                                 migration (ADR-2607010930)\", :engine_dependency_unchanged \"isekai-network still depends on kami-engine as an\\n                                 external engine (a west sibling project) for\\n                                 anything beyond `clojure -M author.clj` --\\n                                 concept 1's WASM compile remains blocked on that\\n                                 migration landing a working kamiclj-equivalent\\n                                 entry point, tracked as it was in PR #91, now\\n                                 tracked from isekai-network's own README instead\", :zero_kami_engine_footprint \"kami-engine's git history has no isekai-network\\n                                commits at all (PR closed unmerged, not merged\\n                                then reverted) -- clean separation\"}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico (game project codename isekai-network) lives at\n    orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network, not nested under kotoba-lang/kami-engine's\n    kami-clj-play/games/" "kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #91 (the initial kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/\n    placement) was closed unmerged, superseded by this split -- kami-engine has\n    zero net footprint from this game project" "the 5-concept EDN game bible (design/00-game-bible.edn + 01..05) and the\n    concept-1 prototype (author.clj/logic.clj, clojure -M author.clj verified\n    working end-to-end) moved verbatim into the new repo's design/ and\n    games/01-netsurvivors/ -- no content changes, only relocation" "the WASM-compile blocker found while authoring the kami-engine PR (kami-engine-clj\n    deleted upstream in kotoba-lang/kotoba PR #259, part of the in-progress\n    clj-wgsl migration, ADR-2607010930) is orthogonal to this repo-placement\n    decision and remains open regardless of where the game code lives")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "isekai-network-split"), (:adr/related (vector "CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011816-ghosthacker-shiropico-standalone-repo.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607010930-clj-wgsl-migration.edn" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #91 (closed, superseded)" "orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607023200-isekai-network-standalone-repo"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-02"), (:adr/body "# ADR 2607023200: isekai-network (Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico game) as a standalone repo, not nested in kami-engine\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/kami-engine` PR #91 held the full deliverable produced so far for\n**Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico** (game project codename `isekai-network`): a\n5-concept EDN game bible (`design/00-game-bible.edn` — title, cast, bestiary,\nshared controls/tone/rating — plus `design/01..05.edn`, one per concept\nvariant) and a real first prototype for concept 1 (熱痕ランナー): `author.clj`\n+ `logic.clj`, a faithful rename/recolour of `kami-clj-play/games/survivors`\nonto the shiro-pico/ghost cast, with `clojure -M author.clj` verified working\nend-to-end. Review found the PR clean (CI green, mergeable, no correctness\nissues).\n\nWhile the PR was open for review, explicit user direction arrived:\n\"個別のゲームは isekai-network repo にまとめてね\" (consolidate the individual\ngames into the isekai-network repo).\n\nThis is the identical structural question ADR-2607011816 already resolved for\nthis franchise's narrative content. That ADR split `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`\nout of `ai-gftd-mangaka` specifically to decouple an independently-lifecycled\nIP from an unrelated engine/infra repo's churn, and to give SHIRO & PICO the\nsame standalone-repo symmetry Ren's Ghost Hacker line already has\n(`orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker`). The same reasoning transfers directly to\nthe game project: `kami-engine` is mid an active internal migration\n(ADR-2607010930, clj-wgsl) that had already deleted the `kami-engine-clj` Rust\ncrate PR #91's own README depended on for its compile instructions — coupling\na product-shaped game's lifecycle to that churn repeats the exact mistake\nADR-2607011816 already named and rejected once for this franchise. Separately,\n`kami-engine`'s own `ARCHITECTURE.md` already treats new games as separate\nper-game crates/repos (the `kami-app-{game}` convention), not nested paths —\na standalone `isekai-network` repo is consistent with that convention too.\n\n## Decision\n\n### New standalone repo, not merged into kami-engine\n\n`orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network` (private, per `repos.edn`'s `gftdcojp` org\ndefault). Contents: a plain copy of the 12 git-tracked files from\n`kami-engine`'s `kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/`, restructured as\n`design/*.edn` (unchanged) + `games/01-netsurvivors/*` (unchanged content;\n`author.clj` re-verified with `clojure -M author.clj` from the new location).\n`git init`, one commit, `gh repo create --source=. --push` — the same pattern\nADR-2607011816 used for `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`.\n\n`kotoba-lang/kami-engine` PR #91 was **closed unmerged**, not merged-then-\nreverted — `kami-engine`'s git history has zero isekai-network commits at\nall. `kami-clj-play/games/{survivors,waves}` and everything else in\n`kami-engine` are unaffected; PR #91 only ever touched the new\n`isekai-network/` subtree.\n\n### Manifest registration via the GitHub Contents API, not a local edit\n\n`manifest/repos.edn`'s `:extra-projects` and `manifest/west.yml` both get one\nnew entry each via a GitHub Contents API single-entry commit (blob-SHA-matched\nPUT against `origin/main` tip) — the same method, and the same reason,\nADR-2607011816 used: this superproject checkout has concurrent-fleet pin drift\nand shallow-clone `(forced update)` noise that make a local edit + full\n`nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs` regen risky (it would bundle unrelated\ndrifted child-repo pins into what should be a one-line registration). Pin is\nverified to equal `orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network@main` HEAD before commit;\n`nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` is run afterward to confirm the\nhand-placed entries match canonical generator output.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- **Symmetry.** Ghost Hacker's three living surfaces now each have the\n  standalone-repo shape ADR-2607011816 established as this franchise's norm:\n  Ren's line (`orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker`), SHIRO & PICO's narrative\n  content (`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`), and now the game\n  project (`orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network`).\n- **Decoupled from engine churn.** `isekai-network`'s lifecycle (design\n  iteration, future concept prototypes) no longer shares a repo, issue\n  tracker, or commit history with `kami-engine`'s in-progress clj-wgsl\n  Rust-removal migration.\n- **Engine dependency unchanged.** `isekai-network` still depends on\n  `kami-engine` as an external engine (a west sibling project) for anything\n  beyond `clojure -M author.clj`. Concept 1's WASM compile remains blocked on\n  that migration landing a working `kamiclj`-equivalent entry point — the\n  same open item PR #91 already documented, now tracked from\n  `isekai-network`'s own README instead.\n- **Zero kami-engine footprint.** Confirmed by closing the PR unmerged rather\n  than merging then reverting.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Merge PR #91 as-is, keep the game nested in `kami-engine`'s\n   `kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/`**: rejected per explicit user\n   direction, and because it repeats the exact coupling-to-unrelated-engine-\n   churn mistake ADR-2607011816 already identified and rejected for this\n   franchise's narrative content.\n2. **Name the new repo `ai-gftd-isekai-network`**, matching gftdcojp's\n   `ai-gftd-*` naming convention (`ai-gftd-mangaka`, `ai-gftd-animeka`,\n   `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`): rejected — the user explicitly requested\n   the literal name \"isekai-network repo\"; honoring the exact requested name\n   over an unrequested convention.\n3. **Merge PR #91 into kami-engine first, then create isekai-network and\n   delete the kami-engine copy in a follow-up commit**: rejected as a\n   needless detour through `kami-engine`'s git history — closing the clean,\n   unmerged PR directly leaves zero trace, matching how ADR-2607012000's\n   abandoned `michibiki` actor-repo detour was handled (deleted before ever\n   landing).\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607011816 (ghosthacker-shiropico standalone repo — the precedent this\n  ADR reuses)\n- ADR-2607010930 (clj-wgsl migration — the churn this split decouples from,\n  and the source of the WASM-compile blocker)\n- ADR-2607012000 (shiropico publish actor — the abandoned-detour handling\n  precedent for alternative 3)\n- `manifest/repos.edn` `:manifest-workflow` (canonical GitHub-API registration\n  path)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine` PR #91 (closed, superseded)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network`"), (:adr/decision "{:new_repo {:path \"orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network\", :remote \"gftdcojp\", :visibility :private, :org_default_visibility_source \"repos.edn :orgs :visibility (gftdcojp = private, per CLAUDE.md standing policy, ADR-2607021330)\", :method \"plain copy of the 12 git-tracked files from kami-engine's\\n                      kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/ -> new repo, restructured\\n                      as design/*.edn (unchanged) + games/01-netsurvivors/* (unchanged\\n                      content, author.clj re-verified with `clojure -M author.clj`\\n                      from the new location), git init, one commit, gh repo create\\n                      --source=. --push (same pattern as ADR-2607011816's\\n                      ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico split)\"}, :source_pr_change {:repo \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine\", :action \"PR #91 closed unmerged (not merged-then-reverted) -- superseded by orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network\", :unaffected \"kami-clj-play/games/{survivors,waves} and all other kami-engine content -- PR #91 only ever touched the new isekai-network/ subtree\"}, :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"add \\\"orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network\\\" to :extra-projects via GitHub\\n               Contents API single-entry commit (blob-sha-matched PUT against\\n               origin/main tip), not a local edit -- same method ADR-2607011816\\n               used, for the same reason: this superproject checkout has\\n               concurrent-fleet pin drift and shallow-clone '(forced update)'\\n               noise that make a local edit + full regen risky\", :west_yml \"add one project entry (name/remote/revision/path/groups),\\n              alphabetically placed, mirroring the ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico\\n              entry's shape, via the same API method\", :why_api_not_local \"identical rationale to ADR-2607011816: avoids a stale-base\\n                        3-way merge against a moving main tip, and avoids bundling\\n                        unrelated drifted child-repo pins into a one-line\\n                        registration commit (the 'pin regression trap' repos.edn's\\n                        :manifest-workflow warns about)\", :verify \"pin == orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network@main HEAD confirmed before commit;\\n            nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check run after to confirm the\\n            hand-placed entries match canonical generator output\"}}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-02: '個別のゲームは isekai-network repo にまとめてね' (consolidate the individual games into the isekai-network repo), sent while kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #91 was open for review\", :investigated [\"PR #91 held the full deliverable so far: design/00-game-bible.edn (title\\n    'Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico', cast, bestiary, shared controls/tone/rating)\\n    + design/01..05.edn (one per concept variant) + a real concept-1 prototype\\n    (author.clj/logic.clj, a faithful rename+recolour of\\n    kami-clj-play/games/survivors onto the shiro-pico/ghost cast) -- review\\n    found it clean (CI green, mergeable) with no correctness issues\" \"ADR-2607011816 already resolved the identical structural question for\\n    this franchise's narrative content: ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico was\\n    split out of ai-gftd-mangaka specifically to decouple an independently-\\n    lifecycled IP from an unrelated engine/infra repo's churn, and to match\\n    the standalone-repo symmetry Ren's Ghost Hacker line already has\\n    (orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker). The same reasoning transfers directly\\n    to the game project: kami-engine is mid an active internal migration\\n    (ADR-2607010930, clj-wgsl, which had already deleted the kami-engine-clj\\n    Rust crate PR #91's own README depended on) -- coupling a product-shaped\\n    game's lifecycle to that churn is the same mistake ADR-2607011816 already\\n    named and rejected once for this franchise\" \"west.yml's own kami-app-{game} convention (ARCHITECTURE.md) already\\n    treats new games as separate per-game crates/repos, not nested paths --\\n    a standalone isekai-network repo is consistent with that convention too,\\n    not just with the shiropico content-split precedent\"], :risk \"PR #91 was clean and mergeable; closing it unmerged rather than\\n         merging-then-deleting avoids ever landing content in kami-engine's\\n         history that would need a follow-up removal commit\"}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"merge PR #91 as-is, keep the game nested in kami-engine's kami-clj-play/games/isekai-network/\", :rejected_because \"explicit user direction to consolidate into a dedicated repo; also repeats the exact coupling-to-unrelated-engine-churn mistake ADR-2607011816 already identified and rejected for this franchise's narrative content\"} {:option \"name the new repo ai-gftd-isekai-network, matching gftdcojp's ai-gftd-* naming convention (ai-gftd-mangaka, ai-gftd-animeka, ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico)\", :rejected_because \"user explicitly requested the literal name 'isekai-network repo' -- honoring the exact requested name over imposing an unrequested naming convention\"} {:option \"merge PR #91 into kami-engine first, then separately create isekai-network and delete the kami-engine copy in a follow-up commit\", :rejected_because \"would leave a needless detour through kami-engine's git history; closing the clean, unmerged PR directly is simpler and leaves zero trace, matching how ADR-2607012000's abandoned michibiki-repo detour was handled (deleted before ever landing, no trace in history)\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607023200: isekai-network (Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico game) as a standalone repo, not nested in kami-engine"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))